Node.js built-in proxy settings are ignored when an HTTP request uses a Unix domain socket. Use `socketPath` instead of `host`/`port`:

```js
const http = require('node:http');

const req = http.request({
  socketPath: '/path/to/socket.sock',
  path: '/',
  method: 'GET'
}, (res) => {
  res.on('data', chunk => process.stdout.write(chunk));
});

req.end();
```

A Unix-socket request therefore connects directly to the socket, not through the configured HTTP(S) proxy.
